vince</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Chikuzen Province was an old province of Japan in northern Kyushu, covering the north-western part of modern Fukuoka Prefecture.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chilarai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chilarai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chilarai</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Chilarai, born Shukladhwaj, was the younger brother and general of the Koch king Nara Narayan in the 16th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/child-sacrifice"><span class="enc-name">Child sacrifice</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Child sacrifice refers to the ritual killing of children as offerings to deities.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/childebert-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Childebert I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Childebert I was a Merovingian king of the Franks who ruled from Paris from 511 to 558.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/childeric-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/childeric-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Childeric I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Childeric I was a king of the Salian Franks, traditionally the son of Merovech, who ruled from Tournai until his death around 481.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chilean-civil-code"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chilean-civil-code.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chilean Civil Code</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Chilean Civil Code, drafted by Andrés Bello and promulgated in December 1855, came into force in 1857.</span></a></li></ul>
